{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":869,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Ps.132","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Psalms","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Psalms 132","reference":"Psalms 132","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"Probably this psalm was wrote by Solomon to be sung at the dedication of the temple, of which he desires God would come and take possession, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"8, 9, 10.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":3,"text":"With these words he concluded his prayer, 2 Chron. vi, 41, 42.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":4,"text":"He pleads David's piety towards God, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":5,"text":"1-7.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":6,"text":"And God's promise to David, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":7,"text":"11-18.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":8,"text":"A song of degrees.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":9,"text":"1.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":10,"text":"Afflictions - All his sufferings for thy sake.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":11,"text":"5.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":12,"text":"Until - Until I have raised an house in which the ark may be put.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":13,"text":"6.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":14,"text":"It - Of the ark.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":15,"text":"Ephratah - In the tribe of Ephraim, which was called also Ephratah.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":16,"text":"Found it - Afterwards we found it in Kirjath- jearim, which signifies a city of woods, in the territory whereof the ark was seated for twenty years.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":17,"text":"7.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":18,"text":"Tabernacles - Into his temple.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":19,"text":"Footstool - The ark, is often said to sit between the cherubim, which were above the ark.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":20,"text":"8.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":21,"text":"Rest - Into thy resting place, the temple so called, Isaiah lxvi, 1, where thou hast now a fixed habitation.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":22,"text":"The ark - The seat of thy powerful and glorious presence.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":23,"text":"10.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":24,"text":"David's sake - In regard of thy promises vouchsafed to David.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":25,"text":"Turn not - Cast me not out of thy presence.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":26,"text":"Of - Of me whom thou hast anointed to be king over thy people.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":27,"text":"16.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":28,"text":"Salvation - With thy saving graces and blessings.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":29,"text":"17.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":30,"text":"There - In Jerusalem.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":31,"text":"To bud - His power and glory to flourish.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":32,"text":"A lamp - A successor to continue forever in his family, as this phrase is expounded 1 Kings xi, 36; xv, 4, and particularly one eminent and glorious light, namely, the Messiah.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Psalms","chapter":132}}